    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "retributive_justice_definition",
      "value": "Retributive justice, which can also be called criminal justice, focuses on how to punish crime. It’s based on the idea that when wrongdoing is committed, the wrongdoer should get a proportionate punishment.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0003",
        "chunk_title": "Retributive justice",
        "chunk_order": 2,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "retributive_justice_infliction",
      "value": "That doesn’t mean the wrongdoer should be subjected to exactly the same ordeal but it needs to be proportionate.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0003",
        "chunk_title": "Retributive justice",
        "chunk_order": 2,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "retributive_justice_indifference",
      "value": "Those who study retributive justice also tend to emphasize the need for indifference, meaning that justice shouldn’t be personal or based on revenge.",
